                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "This game was horrible. First of all there are all of these rules that one has to agree to - EU and all that. They actually say you have to SIGN an agreement to play this game. I never saw where I had to sign but it does say that it connects to their game server for you to play the game. Ridiculous for those of us outside of the EU. Also, one apparently cannot play without connecting to the server. Secondly, it seems to mostly be an online PvP game. There are options to play locally or offline but it's obvious that this game was meant to be an online PvP game. Thirdly, it is very confusing. After playing for about a half an hour and then watching a friend play it, we never understood it completely. It's very confusing to know which piece to choose, why one can't choose other pieces, why one has to pass, etc. Trying to figure out how to flip and turn the pieces wasn't fun, either. Finally, I had to just quit the game because after passing my turn, the game got stuck on itself. I couldn't click away. I couldn't click anywhere. I literally had to kill the game to quit. An abysmal ending. It's a shame. The concept interested me. The graphics looked cozy. Looks are obviously deceiving. :-(",
